# Implementation Plan: Deploying IT Inventory to DeanOS

This plan outlines the steps to replace the current IT Inventory installation on the DeanOS server (`192.168.1.186`) with the updated "premium" version from the local workspace.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The deployment will involve restarting the `it-inventory` Docker container on the server. This will result in a brief downtime (approx. 30-60 seconds).
>
> [!WARNING]
> We will be syncing the `/DATA/dean/projects/My-Personal-Repository/` directory on the server. A full backup will be created before any changes are applied.

## Proposed Changes

### IT Inventory Deployment [DeanOS]

1.  **Preparation**:
    - [x] Verify local repository status (`C:\projects\it-inventory`).
    - [x] Identify deployment path on server: `/DATA/projects/it-inventory`.
2.  **Server Cleanup**:
    - [x] SSH into DeanOS (`192.168.1.186`).
    - [x] Remove existing container `it-inventory` (if any).
    - [x] Remove old project directory `/DATA/projects/it-inventory` (if any).
3.  **Fresh Deployment**:
    - [x] Clone the repository: `git clone https://github.com/evatechnosoft/My-Personal-Repository.git /DATA/projects/it-inventory`.
    - [x] Create `.env` from `.env.example` and configure `APP_BASE_URL`.
    - [x] Build and start the service: `sudo docker compose up -d --build app`.
    - [ ] Set final permissions: `sudo chown -R dean:samba /DATA/projects/it-inventory`.
4.  **Verification**:
    - [x] Check container logs: `sudo docker logs it-inventory`.
    - [ ] Confirm web access: `http://192.168.1.186:8001`.
    - [ ] Test UI buttons ("Add New Device", "Add Request").

---

### Phase 2: BigBear Coolify Installation & Configuration

1.  **Preparation [DeanOS]**:
    - Identify existing BigBear Coolify directory: `/DATA/AppData/big-bear-coolify`.
    - Locate CasaOS app definition: `/var/lib/casaos/apps/big-bear-coolify/docker-compose.yml`.
2.  **Service Activation**:
    - [ ] Run `docker compose up -d` in the app directory.
    - [ ] Monitor logs for `big-bear-coolify` and `big-bear-coolify-postgres`.
    - [ ] Resolve any port conflicts (default: 8000).
3.  **SSH Infrastructure**:
    - [ ] Configure `coolify` to use the provided `coolos.pub` for host management.
4.  **Local SSH Config**:
    - [ ] Add the following to `C:\Users\Deacjx\.ssh\config`:
      ```text
      Host coolos
          HostName 192.168.1.186
          User dean
          Port 8000 (UI) / 22 (SSH)
          IdentityFile C:\Users\Deacjx\.ssh\coolos
      ```
5.  **Verification**:
    - [ ] Access UI: `http://192.168.1.186:8000`.
    - [ ] Perform initial administrative setup.

---

### Phase 3: UI Interactivity & Layout Polish

#### 1. Resolve Stacking Context (Click Blocking)
- **Problem**: `backdrop-filter` and `animation` on containers are trapping modals in a lower stacking context, causing the backdrop to block clicks.
-   **[MODIFY] [base.html](file:///C:/projects/it-inventory/templates/base.html)**:
    - Add `{% block modals %}{% endblock %}` at the very end of `<body>`, outside of `container-fluid`.
    - Reduce `.navbar` z-index to `1000` (below modals but above content).
-   **[MODIFY] [inventory.html](file:///C:/projects/it-inventory/templates/inventory.html)** & **[requests.html](file:///C:/projects/it-inventory/templates/requests.html)**:
    - Move modal code to the newly created `modals` block.

#### 2. Layout Optimization (Cramping Fixes)
-   **[MODIFY] [style.css](file:///C:/projects/it-inventory/static/style.css)**:
    - Increase `gap` in `.dashboard-grid` and card rows.
    - Adjust `.navbar` padding and dropdown behavior to prevent "cramped" look.
    - Ensure `.stats-card` (adetler) have better padding and responsive behavior.
-   **[MODIFY] [inventory.html](file:///C:/projects/it-inventory/templates/inventory.html)**:
    - Improve the "Stats" and "Filter Form" rows for better spacing.
    - Add `table-responsive` explicitly where needed.

#### 3. Verification
- Access `http://192.168.1.186:8001/inventory/`.
- Verify the modal can be interacted with using the mouse.
- Confirm dashboard stats and Excel buttons look premium and spaced out.

